WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.130
This is east Purbeck.

2
00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.330
Follow the shoreline, and it zigzags.

3
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.950
Durlston Head juts out.

4
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.230
Swanage Bay curves in.

5
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.110
Ballard Point juts out.

6
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.330
Studland Bay curves in.

7
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.750
Same sea, same storms.

8
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.510
So why does one stretch of rock jut
out, while the next curves into a bay?

9
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.590
Did rivers carve the bays?

10
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.250
In this mission, you'll map
the rocks along the coast,

11
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.570
and see how their pattern
shapes the shoreline.

12
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.770
Then you'll follow waves
as they reach the coast,

13
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.610
and track where their energy goes.

14
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:38.290
Your mission: explain why one rock juts
out as a headland while its neighbour

15
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.810
curves into a bay.
